From: Alienware Control Center for Linux research
Subject: [RFC DO NOT MERGE] hwmon: (dell-smm) add experimental x17 R1 fan control

This is an offline research candidate only. The 0x34a3/0x35a3 pair has not
been verified on the target machine. Do not submit or load without a controlled
hardware test and a confirmed recovery path.

An independent x17 R1 boot log shows dell-bios-fan-control being executed; the
published source of that utility uses 0x34a3/0x35a3. However, that utility
ignores the SMM return status and always prints success, so this is evidence of
an attempted command only, not proof that the firmware accepted it.

--- a/drivers/hwmon/dell-smm-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/dell-smm-hwmon.c
@@ -1549,6 +1549,14 @@ static const struct i8k_fan_control_data i8k_fan_control_data[] __initconst = {
 };
 
 static const struct dmi_system_id i8k_whitelist_fan_control[] __initconst = {
+	{
+		.ident = "Alienware x17 R1 (experimental)",
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Alienware"),
+			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "Alienware x17 R1"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = (void *)&i8k_fan_control_data[I8K_FAN_34A3_35A3],
+	},
 	{
 		.ident = "Dell G5 5505",
 		.matches = {
